  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nStill expecting periods of light precipitation across mainly eastern \nzones as a shortwave and associated low move northeast along the \ncoast. Expecting only light precipitation, as this feature continues \na more easterly track, and somewhat dry air continues to linger \nacross the region. Otherwise, focus shifts to a trough and \nassociated cold front that will approach from the west later \ntonight. This will spread light precipitation into the area, along \nwith cooler temperatures to start the week, with little diurnal \nchange in temperatures expected for Monday. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...\n\nActive weather returns to the area mid to late week as two defined \nshortwaves, one across the Southern Plains and another digging \nsoutheast out of the Upper Midwest into the Mid-Mississippi Valley \nregion develop, with the southern stream wave spurring a low that \nwill ride northeast along the eastern seaboard and eventually \ntowards our area, with the two features eventually phasing over our \narea. Much of the precipitation should fall in the form of rain, \nalthough periods of a wintry mix are possible across the mountains \nat times. As the low pulls off to the northeast on Friday, mainly \nlingering precipitation in the mountains will remain, and depending \non evolution/path, could result in a wintry mix for Friday across \nnorthern mountains, but no rush of cold air is anticipated at this \ntime. In addition to the precipitation, windy conditions are \nexpected to take hold during the period, but advisory level \nconditions are not anticipated at this time.",
